title: Discard every change while two files have unsaved text (one changed on disk, one not): both are as committed on disk and on the canvas, the untracked file survives, quitting asks nothing
folders: git-changes
expect-file: git-changes/src/steps.rs :: ^fn step_1\(\) -> u32 \{\n    1\n\}\n\nfn step_2\(\) -> u32 \{\n    2\n\}[\s\S]*fn step_6\(\)[\s\S]*\n    11\n
expect-file: git-changes/src/util.rs :: ^pub fn double\(n: u32\) -> u32 \{\n    n \* 2\n
expect-file: git-changes/src/new_file.rs :: fresh
forbid-log: script: ignoring
forbid-log: nothing offers
forbid-log: script: Answer\("Close

wait 3000
left changes
edit src/steps.rs 1 1
type // one
key enter
edit src/util.rs 1 1
type // two
key enter
wait 800
mark typed
wait 500
git discard
wait 600
mark asked
wait 500
answer Discard
wait 2000
mark end
wait 500
quit
wait 1000
answer Close without saving
wait 800
